course: dictionary
lesson: 15517
title: Subsidence: when the ground sinks
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Subsidence means the ground slowly sinks lower. Think of a sandcastle on the beach: when the wet sand underneath washes away, the top part sinks. Real land can do this too, and it can take months or years.
explain: Look at the clues around the word in this sentence: «Cracks appeared in the walls after subsidence under the house.» Cracks and walls show damage, and "under the house" tells you something below is moving. So subsidence must mean the ground sinking.
explain: The word can also mean something dying down, such as a flood or storm easing off: «After the subsidence of the flood, the roads were dry again.» Swap in "sinking" or "dying down" and check which one still makes sense in the sentence.
fact: Subsidence means the ground slowly sinks lower.
fact: Common causes of subsidence are old mines underneath, soil drying out, groundwater being removed, and soft ground.
fact: «Subsidence damage» can crack houses, roads and walls.
fact: Subsidence is an uncountable noun, so we say "some subsidence", not "subsidences".
fact: Subsidence can also mean a flood, storm or feeling dying down.
exercise: «Cracks appeared in the walls because of subsidence.» What does subsidence mean here? | A loud noise from the sky | A type of bright paint | A hot summer wind | *The ground slowly sinks lower
exercise: «The engineer said the crack was caused by mining subsidence.» What might cause mining subsidence? | *Old mines underneath the land | A rainbow after the rain | Heavy snow on the roof | A new swimming pool in the garden
exercise: «After the subsidence of the flood, the streets were dry again.» What does subsidence mean in this sentence? | A new road was being built | The ground under the streets was sinking | *The flood was dying down | The water was rising higher
test: «Homeowners checked for subsidence damage after the dry summer.» What might the dry summer have done? | Melted the snow on the mountains | Made the sky turn green | Filled the rivers to the top | *Dried out the soil so the ground sank
test: Choose the correct sentence. | The house had many subsidences. | The house had three subsidences. | *The house had some subsidence.
exam: A family finds cracks in their kitchen wall after the ground under their house slowly sinks. What is this called? | Ventilation | Pollution | Celebration | *Subsidence
